Program the vendor rknand per-page randomizer seed on WRITE so pages we program
are scrambled the same way the read path (patch 0002) expects to descramble them.

Mainline leaves the randomizer off on the program path, so pages it writes are
unscrambled and cannot be read back by rk_nfc_read_page_hwecc (which now programs
the seed) nor by a vendor/FTL-compatible reader. This patch makes the write path
symmetric to the read path: it programs the same per-page seed
(rk_nand_randmz_seed[page & 0x7f] | 0xc0000000 into RANDMZ_CFG) before the NFC
write transfer, for every non-boot page. The 40-bit BCH parity is still generated
by the controller hardware, unchanged.

Because rk_nand_randmz_seed[] is defined further down (just before the read path),
a forward declaration is added so the earlier write function can reference it.

Round-trip verified with tools/nand-write-test.py: erase a verified-free block,
write a known pattern through this path, read it back through patch 0002 — the
bytes match. Safe to test on this box because it boots from SD independently, so a
bad NAND write cannot brick it.

--- a/drivers/mtd/nand/raw/rockchip-nand-controller.c
+++ b/drivers/mtd/nand/raw/rockchip-nand-controller.c
@@ before rk_nfc_write_page_hwecc() @@
+/* Defined below; used by both the write (scramble) and read (descramble) paths. */
+static const u16 rk_nand_randmz_seed[128];
+
 static int rk_nfc_write_page_hwecc(struct nand_chip *chip, const u8 *buf,
 				   int oob_on, int page)
 {
@@ in rk_nfc_write_page_hwecc(), after the oob DMA mapping, before xfer_start @@
 	dma_oob = dma_map_single(nfc->dev, nfc->oob_buf,
 				 ecc->steps * oob_step,
 				 DMA_TO_DEVICE);

+	/* s3plus: program the RE'd vendor per-page randomizer seed so the NFC
+	 * hardware scrambles data pages on write, symmetric to the read path
+	 * (mainline leaves it off). Same seed table indexed by page & 0x7f,
+	 * enabled by OR'ing 0xc0000000 into RANDMZ_CFG. This makes pages we
+	 * write vendor-format readable by rk_nfc_read_page_hwecc and, later, a
+	 * vendor/FTL-compatible reader. */
+	if (!boot_rom_mode)
+		writel(rk_nand_randmz_seed[page & 0x7f] | 0xc0000000,
+		       nfc->regs + nfc->cfg->randmz_off);
+
 	reinit_completion(&nfc->done);
 	writel(INT_DMA, nfc->regs + nfc->cfg->int_en_off);

 	rk_nfc_xfer_start(nfc, NFC_WRITE, ecc->steps, dma_data,
 			  dma_oob);
